        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(admin-http-rpc): reject oversized declared request bodies",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nFixes an issue where Admin HTTP RPC callers could send oversized JSON request bodies and lose the structured 413 response when the request exceeded the 1 MiB route limit.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nThe Admin HTTP RPC handler now rejects oversized declared `Content-Length` values before reading the body. For streamed overflow, it preserves the structured 413 response and closes the request immediately after that response has been handed to the operating system, so a sender that keeps transmitting cannot retain the request in flowing mode.\n\n## User Impact\n\nOperators and host tooling using `POST /api/v1/admin/rpc` get a clear HTTP 413 JSON response for oversized declared or streamed request bodies. Invalid oversized requests do not reach Gateway RPC dispatch, and continued chunked uploads are closed after the response.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- Current-head repair: at `efe8cbd64663006af0f138d5243bb779b7a4f4dd`, the streamed-overflow branch closes the request after the 413 response `finish` event instead of leaving the oversized upload in flowing mode.\n- Current-head GitHub proof: `Real behavior proof` passed for `efe8cbd64663006af0f138d5243bb779b7a4f4dd` (https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/actions/runs/29592790433/job/87925748028), exercising the Admin HTTP RPC oversized-body behavior.\n- Regression coverage: `extensions/admin-http-rpc/src/handler.test.ts` uses a real Node HTTP client that exceeds the limit, keeps writing, receives the structured 413, and observes the connection close.\n- Diff scope: `gh pr diff 104552 --repo openclaw/openclaw --name-only` shows the current PR diff is limited to `extensions/admin-http-rpc/src/handler.ts` and `extensions/admin-http-rpc/src/handler.test.ts`.\n\nAI-assisted: yes. I reviewed the Admin HTTP RPC route boundary, Node stream iterator contract, response-finish cleanup path, and ClawSweeper feedback before updating this PR.",
